import{_ as a,o as t,c as r,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.BdWD-ld-.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence · 2026-11-25","description":"45 observations and 6 analyses on authority evidence, recovery and digital-employee SOP handoff.","frontmatter":{"title":"Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence · 2026-11-25","description":"45 observations and 6 analyses on authority evidence, recovery and digital-employee SOP handoff."},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-25.md","filePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-25.md","lastUpdated":1795572940000}'),i={name:"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-25.md"};function o(s,e,l,d,c,p){return t(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="agent-research-and-competitor-intelligence-·-2026-11-25" tabindex="-1">Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence · 2026-11-25 <a class="header-anchor" href="#agent-research-and-competitor-intelligence-·-2026-11-25" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence · 2026-11-25&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The strongest research thread is preserving task-governing rules, authority and action/delivery evidence across handoff, cancellation, recovery and upgrades. Forty-five observations support six analyses. Priority candidates are real-agent SOP migration/independent review and recovery under unknown external outcomes. Releases, merges and proposals remain distinct. Zero new experiments, articles, development reviews or comments in this monitoring run.</p><p>Run date uses Asia/Shanghai; commit-window cutoff：2026-11-25T02:04:12Z。Other PR states were verified when read this round. Source timestamps below use UTC; date-only announcements retain their original dates. Not all events occurred on Nov25 Shanghai time. Yesterday&#39;s successful report exists; no backdated reports are invented.</p><h2 id="factual-observations" tabindex="-1">Factual observations <a class="header-anchor" href="#factual-observations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Factual observations&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="o1-·-claude-ships-mcp-workflow-support" tabindex="-1">O1 · Claude ships MCP workflow support <a class="header-anchor" href="#o1-·-claude-ships-mcp-workflow-support" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O1 · Claude ships MCP workflow support&quot;">​</a></h3><p>On Nov 24, Claude announced Skills over MCP beta (default for Pro/Max/Ultra; Team admin opt-in; Enterprise forthcoming), GA Tasks/Elicitation on individual paid plans with organizational rollout, and forthcoming file uploads. This is client delivery, not a newly invented protocol; an untested workflow integration candidate.</p><p><a href="https://claude.com/resources/articles/skills-over-mcp-tasks-and-more" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official product announcement</a> — <strong>ANNOUNCED / BETA / GA / COMING_SOON</strong> · 2026-11-24</p><h3 id="o2-·-claude-code-adds-pre-skill-controls-and-failure-visibility" tabindex="-1">O2 · Claude Code adds pre-skill controls and failure visibility <a class="header-anchor" href="#o2-·-claude-code-adds-pre-skill-controls-and-failure-visibility" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O2 · Claude Code adds pre-skill controls and failure visibility&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Released v2.1.332 adds PreSkillShellCommand refusal for inline skill shell commands; older versions show a startup dialog for that setting. It fixes SSE MCP reconnection and unbounded-hook hangs and warns about incomplete persistence or missing resumed history. Warnings do not establish recovery guarantees.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.332" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v2.1.332</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-25T01:32:14Z</p><h3 id="o3-·-codex-binds-refreshed-mcp-credentials-to-session-ownership" tabindex="-1">O3 · Codex binds refreshed MCP credentials to session ownership <a class="header-anchor" href="#o3-·-codex-binds-refreshed-mcp-credentials-to-session-ownership" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O3 · Codex binds refreshed MCP credentials to session ownership&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Extensions can provide fresh headers per request for host-local Streamable HTTP MCP. Same-owner rotation reuses a session; owner mismatch is rejected and changed ownership rebuilds it. Redirects are disabled and shared startup catalogs bypassed. A main-branch integration candidate, not verified released functionality.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63532" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63532 Let extensions supply per-request authentication for MCP servers</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T04:08:55Z</p><h3 id="o4-·-codex-binds-reviews-to-actions-and-parent-evidence" tabindex="-1">O4 · Codex binds reviews to actions and parent evidence <a class="header-anchor" href="#o4-·-codex-binds-reviews-to-actions-and-parent-evidence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O4 · Codex binds reviews to actions and parent evidence&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The experimental review API takes an explicit toolCall without executing it; native action framing is off by default. Trusted hosts supply root instructions, recheck evidence and invalidate caches on root replacement. Cached scores must match action and worker/root revisions. Recorded reviews require idle ephemeral non-subagent threads and reset history when evidence changes. First verdict guidance requires reading user instructions.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63513" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63513 Direct Guardian to read user instructions before its first verdict</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T03:11:57Z； <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63654" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63654 Accept an explicit tool call in Guardian review requests</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T14:36:17Z； <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63649" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63649 Frame pending native agent calls as Guardian approval requests</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T14:20:53Z； <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63742" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63742 Use root evidence in Guardian reviews for hosted agents</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T21:12:05Z； <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63770" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63770 Include parent evidence in recorded Guardian reviews</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T23:56:52Z</p><h3 id="o5-·-codex-waits-for-durable-revocation-evidence" tabindex="-1">O5 · Codex waits for durable revocation evidence <a class="header-anchor" href="#o5-·-codex-waits-for-durable-revocation-evidence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O5 · Codex waits for durable revocation evidence&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Before review cutoff, root-history appends must be acknowledged; unconfirmed writes fail preparation and request reload/resend. Tracked evidence persists in order after caller cancellation and drains on shutdown; accepted user answers are recorded before waking the tool. History gaps remain explicit. This does not prove generic crash durability.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63675" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63675 Wait for pending history writes before Guardian v3 reviews</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T16:47:29Z； <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63693" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63693 Preserve Guardian review evidence when callers are cancelled</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T17:34:04Z</p><h3 id="o6-·-codex-aligns-retries-and-resumed-approval-settings" tabindex="-1">O6 · Codex aligns retries and resumed approval settings <a class="header-anchor" href="#o6-·-codex-aligns-retries-and-resumed-approval-settings" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O6 · Codex aligns retries and resumed approval settings&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Unsandboxed retries require explicit escalation review; sandbox-required retries retain read restrictions. Saved allow rules do not widen denied reads automatically. Exec restores approval policy/reviewer and refuses interactive-human requests in noninteractive mode. resume --approve-for-me affects only initial resume and fails when settings or restrictions cannot be verified.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63683" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63683 Align sandbox retries with the permissions reviewed for them</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T17:20:16Z； <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63743" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63743 Review saved exec escalations when read denials apply</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T21:27:54Z； <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63515" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63515 Honor configured and saved approvals in <code>codex exec</code></a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T03:13:50Z； <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63589" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63589 Scope <code>resume --approve-for-me</code> to the initial conversation</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T09:35:59Z</p><h3 id="o7-·-codex-ties-proxy-access-to-granted-ports-and-prepared-routes" tabindex="-1">O7 · Codex ties proxy access to granted ports and prepared routes <a class="header-anchor" href="#o7-·-codex-ties-proxy-access-to-granted-ports-and-prepared-routes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O7 · Codex ties proxy access to granted ports and prepared routes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Linux managed proxy bridges require loopbackPorts grants; an empty list creates none even under full access. Generated CA access is captured and validated with the prepared route rather than mutable live settings. Explicit local binding and Unix-socket rights remain separate. Relevant to call-time authorization and drift.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63775" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63775 Require port grants for Linux sandbox proxy bridges</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-25T00:12:53Z； <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63711" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63711 Bind sandbox CA access to the prepared managed proxy route</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T18:52:16Z</p><h3 id="o8-·-codex-reconnects-expired-mcp-sessions-without-replay" tabindex="-1">O8 · Codex reconnects expired MCP sessions without replay <a class="header-anchor" href="#o8-·-codex-reconnects-expired-mcp-sessions-without-replay" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O8 · Codex reconnects expired MCP sessions without replay&quot;">​</a></h3><p>A 404 replying to elicitation closes the expired transport and fails in-flight calls without replay. The next operation reconnects within its deadline; another 404 does not loop. Failed/cancelled handshake sessions are cleaned up where possible. This avoids blind replay without implying remote rollback.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63782" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63782 Recover when an MCP reply hits an expired HTTP session</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-25T00:56:15Z</p><h3 id="o9-·-codex-separates-signing-key-purposes" tabindex="-1">O9 · Codex separates signing-key purposes <a class="header-anchor" href="#o9-·-codex-separates-signing-key-purposes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O9 · Codex separates signing-key purposes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Eval and release signing-key lists enforce their distinct purposes and reject duplicate IDs across lists. Caches are scoped to endpoint and authentication; tampering blocks installation. This extends yesterday&#39;s signature work but does not establish behavioral trust or remove previously observed unsigned compatibility.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63528" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#63528 Verify eval plugin archives with scoped signing keys</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T03:57:01Z</p><h3 id="o10-·-agents-python-promotes-governance-fixes-into-stable-0-26-0" tabindex="-1">O10 · Agents Python promotes governance fixes into stable 0.26.0 <a class="header-anchor" href="#o10-·-agents-python-promotes-governance-fixes-into-stable-0-26-0" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O10 · Agents Python promotes governance fixes into stable 0.26.0&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Stable v0.26.0 includes queued-tool rejection handling, handoff-history redaction, Docker storage restrictions, application image approval and Realtime checks/tracing. Some Docker sessions need replacement with revised manifests and snapshot restoration; RunState/Session schemas are unchanged. Distinct from alpha.2 and subsequent feature-branch work.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/releases/tag/v0.26.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v0.26.0</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-24T03:15:47Z</p><h3 id="o11-·-agents-python-merges-two-result-editors-on-its-feature-branch" tabindex="-1">O11 · Agents Python merges two result editors on its feature branch <a class="header-anchor" href="#o11-·-agents-python-merges-two-result-editors-on-its-feature-branch" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O11 · Agents Python merges two result editors on its feature branch&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Previously OPEN #6141 and #6133 merged into feat/simple-codex after alpha.2, with no newer release verified. Runner transforms bind exact function/server objects and edit text before publication; native transforms replace whole MCP results and must cover structuredContent/_meta, rejecting Core rollout tracing. Re-register on resume; completed effects and other logs/media remain outside the guarantee.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6141" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#6141 Edit text in selected Runner tool results before tracing and publication</a> — <strong>MERGED → feat/simple-codex</strong> · 2026-11-24T16:40:36Z； <a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6133" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#6133 Transform selected native MCP results before publication</a> — <strong>MERGED → feat/simple-codex</strong> · 2026-11-24T16:45:34Z</p><h3 id="o12-·-agents-python-rechecks-specialist-authorization-on-resume" tabindex="-1">O12 · Agents Python rechecks specialist authorization on resume <a class="header-anchor" href="#o12-·-agents-python-rechecks-specialist-authorization-on-resume" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O12 · Agents Python rechecks specialist authorization on resume&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Previously OPEN #6132 merged on feat/simple-codex. Decisions receives explicit routing input/eligible labels; the model chooses when to hand off and Decisions selects an eligible specialist. Permissions are checked before selection/transfer and approval resume. Default 30-second deadline, no fallback on failure; usage is outside Runner budgets. A classifier is not the authority source.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6132" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#6132 Share typed Decisions across agents, callbacks and specialist handoffs</a> — <strong>MERGED → feat/simple-codex</strong> · 2026-11-24T19:40:34Z</p><h3 id="o13-·-agents-python-gates-native-delegation-explicitly" tabindex="-1">O13 · Agents Python gates native delegation explicitly <a class="header-anchor" href="#o13-·-agents-python-gates-native-delegation-explicitly" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O13 · Agents Python gates native delegation explicitly&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Feature-branch #6138 defaults native delegation off without a per-provider children grant. Spawn/resume/send and wait/close have distinct cumulative allowances; failures count and closure refunds nothing. Native children share model, reasoning and permissions. Limits do not cap tokens/spend or ordinary Agent.as_tool budgets; release inclusion unverified.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6138" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#6138 Require an explicit grant for native Codex delegation and bound child attempts</a> — <strong>MERGED → feat/simple-codex</strong> · 2026-11-24T16:34:48Z</p><h3 id="o14-·-agents-python-makes-a2a-uncertainty-explicit" tabindex="-1">O14 · Agents Python makes A2A uncertainty explicit <a class="header-anchor" href="#o14-·-agents-python-makes-a2a-uncertainty-explicit" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O14 · Agents Python makes A2A uncertainty explicit&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Feature-branch #6123 adds an optional A2A client returning Message or Task, checking IDs and separating card/RPC token providers. It sends once without automatic polling/cancellation/retry; timeout leaves outcome unknown. Recovery needs a Task, trusted receipt, cooperating service and current grant; a message ID alone does not deduplicate effects. An FCoP adapter candidate, not a same-layer replacement.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6123" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#6123 Add an optional A2A client for messages and tasks</a> — <strong>MERGED → feat/simple-codex</strong> · 2026-11-24T23:02:10Z</p><h3 id="o15-·-shared-budgets-and-preflight-remain-proposals" tabindex="-1">O15 · Shared budgets and preflight remain proposals <a class="header-anchor" href="#o15-·-shared-budgets-and-preflight-remain-proposals" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O15 · Shared budgets and preflight remain proposals&quot;">​</a></h3><p>OPEN stacked PRs #6211/#6212 propose shared tool/delegation limits and execution-policy preflight; full checks remain incomplete. Preflight cannot verify remote grants, and native spending/shared Codex child budgets are excluded. #6208 steering/queue is CLOSED_UNMERGED, not delivered; its draft receipt only denotes adapter submission, not provider receipt or an answer.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6211" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#6211 Extend RunBudget with shared tool and delegation limits</a> — <strong>OPEN</strong> · state checked this round； <a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6212" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#6212 Add model request preflight and explicit tool execution policies</a> — <strong>OPEN</strong> · state checked this round； <a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6208" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#6208 Steer an active run and queue follow-up messages</a> — <strong>CLOSED_UNMERGED</strong> · state checked this round</p><h3 id="o16-·-community-asks-for-verifiable-mcp-actor-identity" tabindex="-1">O16 · Community asks for verifiable MCP actor identity <a class="header-anchor" href="#o16-·-community-asks-for-verifiable-mcp-actor-identity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O16 · Community asks for verifiable MCP actor identity&quot;">​</a></h3><p>New Nov 24 OPEN issue #6215 reports unchanged bearer credentials across triage/specialist handoff; an app-supplied agent label is not verifiable identity. The author reports 35/35 same-token scripted trials and 7/7 distinguishable token-exchange controls. A community request, not a maintainer-confirmed universal MCP defect or local reproduction.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/issues/6215" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Actor identity after handoff</a> — <strong>OPEN / COMMUNITY_REPORT</strong> · 2026-11-24T14:21:33Z</p><h3 id="o17-·-adk-fixes-cancellation-propagation-and-trace-credential-filtering" tabindex="-1">O17 · ADK fixes cancellation propagation and trace credential filtering <a class="header-anchor" href="#o17-·-adk-fixes-cancellation-propagation-and-trace-credential-filtering" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O17 · ADK fixes cancellation propagation and trace credential filtering&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Default-branch changes propagate runner-originated CancelledError through A2A and filter secret_key/passwd variants from tracing spans where debug logs already redacted them. Release 2.15.1 lists earlier persistence/routing fixes; inclusion of these newer commits is unverified. Control-flow and telemetry confidentiality require separate checks.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/50961696a49750c1bff354c9406c455778c2a166" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">fix(a2a): propagate CancelledError raised inside runner.run_async</a> — <strong>COMMITTED → default branch</strong> · 2026-11-24T16:41:23Z； <a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/e3dbdc1726bed0bfc3d2e3f335fc7c0dcdf6b9c5" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">fix(plugins): keep secret_key and passwd args out of tracing spans</a> — <strong>COMMITTED → default branch</strong> · 2026-11-24T10:33:12Z； <a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/releases/tag/v2.15.1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v2.15.1</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-25T01:01:43Z</p><h3 id="o18-·-langgraph-creates-message-ids-before-persistence" tabindex="-1">O18 · LangGraph creates message IDs before persistence <a class="header-anchor" href="#o18-·-langgraph-creates-message-ids-before-persistence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O18 · LangGraph creates message IDs before persistence&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#9772 assigns IDs before checkpoint persistence for add_messages writes and StateGraph input, stabilizing replay/fork/resume identity. Updates/history representations change; strings and role/content pairs may become message objects, affecting exact-match consumers. Stable message identity is not exactly-once external execution.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/pull/9772" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#9772 fix(langgraph): give add_messages writes and StateGraph input message ids before they are saved</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T20:11:25Z</p><h3 id="o19-·-langgraph-streams-tool-only-progress-live" tabindex="-1">O19 · LangGraph streams tool-only progress live <a class="header-anchor" href="#o19-·-langgraph-streams-tool-only-progress-live" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O19 · LangGraph streams tool-only progress live&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#9779 starts the stream waiter for tools-only mode in sync/async execution, avoiding buffered delivery until node completion. Upstream timing changed from all events at ~0.61s to progressive delivery. Not locally reproduced; visibility helps supervision but does not establish durable recovery.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/pull/9779" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#9779 fix(langgraph): stream tool events live with stream_mode=&quot;tools&quot; alone</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T15:38:32Z</p><h3 id="o20-·-openhands-sdk-hardens-persisted-event-recovery" tabindex="-1">O20 · OpenHands SDK hardens persisted event recovery <a class="header-anchor" href="#o20-·-openhands-sdk-hardens-persisted-event-recovery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O20 · OpenHands SDK hardens persisted event recovery&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#7081 fsyncs the parent directory after POSIX rename and invalidates event counts on sync failure. #7080 isolates unreadable records in broken_items and permits lease-protected deletion while preserving workspaces. Both are listed in released v1.64.0. Upstream deletion-based missing-file tests are not full power-loss validation.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/7081" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#7081 fix(sdk): make event file renames durable across restarts</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T09:37:44Z； <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/7080" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#7080 fix(agent-server): isolate unreadable conversations in history</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T09:29:19Z； <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/releases/tag/v1.64.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v1.64.0</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-24T16:41:28Z</p><h3 id="o21-·-openhands-keeps-parents-active-while-waiting-for-children" tabindex="-1">O21 · OpenHands keeps parents active while waiting for children <a class="header-anchor" href="#o21-·-openhands-keeps-parents-active-while-waiting-for-children" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O21 · OpenHands keeps parents active while waiting for children&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#7105 periodically refreshes idle activity during active runs so parents waiting on Task children are not paused as idle. Native interrupted children can outlive the parent&#39;s heartbeat; atomic pause remains separate. Merged after v1.64.0, so not claimed included in that release.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/7105" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#7105 Keep the agent-server idle timer fresh during active runs</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T20:56:44Z</p><h3 id="o22-·-openhands-decouples-slow-webhooks-from-run-completion" tabindex="-1">O22 · OpenHands decouples slow webhooks from run completion <a class="header-anchor" href="#o22-·-openhands-decouples-slow-webhooks-from-run-completion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O22 · OpenHands decouples slow webhooks from run completion&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#5972 posts full webhook batches in a serialized background sender, allowing completion before a slow receiver responds; close drains pending batches. Final events may arrive after the next run starts. Merged after v1.64.0. Consumers must correlate run/sequence rather than delivery order.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/5972" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#5972 fix(agent-server): post full webhook batches off the event&#39;s publish</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T21:23:35Z</p><h3 id="o23-·-openhands-isolates-state-lock-waiters-from-tool-execution" tabindex="-1">O23 · OpenHands isolates state-lock waiters from tool execution <a class="header-anchor" href="#o23-·-openhands-isolates-state-lock-waiters-from-tool-execution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O23 · OpenHands isolates state-lock waiters from tool execution&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#6933 separates sequential tool execution and per-conversation state-lock operations from the default executor, preventing lock-waiter starvation from freezing unrelated event reads while /alive stays healthy. Isolation adds thread-resource costs. Merged on main; release inclusion not independently established.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6933" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#6933 fix(agent-server): keep state-lock waiters off the default executor</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T16:24:54Z</p><h3 id="o24-·-openhands-releases-project-and-coordination-surfaces" tabindex="-1">O24 · OpenHands releases project and coordination surfaces <a class="header-anchor" href="#o24-·-openhands-releases-project-and-coordination-surfaces" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O24 · OpenHands releases project and coordination surfaces&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Application v1.45.0 ships experimental Projects Canvas, project files/PR context, nested subagents and factory worklogs. SDK v1.64.0 lists project/coordinator/board/artifact APIs and failed-judge escalation without coordinator auto-resolution. A runnable application candidate, not locally installed or enterprise-maturity proof.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/OpenHands/releases/tag/v1.45.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v1.45.0</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-24T09:13:54Z； <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/releases/tag/v1.64.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v1.64.0</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-24T16:41:28Z</p><h3 id="o25-·-staffdeck-separates-sop-distribution-from-grants" tabindex="-1">O25 · StaffDeck separates SOP distribution from grants <a class="header-anchor" href="#o25-·-staffdeck-separates-sop-distribution-from-grants" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O25 · StaffDeck separates SOP distribution from grants&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#325 shares validated SOP requirements without grants or connection settings; copies/syncs check recipient configuration and remain disabled with actionable warnings when requirements are unmet. Identical content reuses publication; unsupported imports fail explicitly; HTTP DTO schema is forwarded. Upstream synthetic/smoke evidence only. High governance learning value; keep main radar without claiming overall maturity.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenBMB/StaffDeck/pull/325" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#325 fix(sop): share gallery templates without granting tools</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T03:54:09Z</p><h3 id="o26-·-paperclip-extends-access-revocation-to-retained-copies" tabindex="-1">O26 · Paperclip extends access revocation to retained copies <a class="header-anchor" href="#o26-·-paperclip-extends-access-revocation-to-retained-copies" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O26 · Paperclip extends access revocation to retained copies&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#22836 triggers durable Google-content deletion on access end, waiting for pre-cutoff work and retrying failed steps, not on transient network failures. #22842 extends cleanup across errors, continuations/handoffs, native results and snapshots, adds a 30-day technical-information sweep and excludes training/feedback exports. Engineering facts only; underlying legal compliance is not independently adjudicated. High learning/competitive relevance; deletion latency and audit-retention tradeoffs remain untested.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22836" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#22836 feat(google): delete content read from Google when access ends</a> — <strong>MERGED → master</strong> · 2026-11-25T00:32:13Z； <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22842" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#22842 feat(google): keep Google Technical Information at most 30 days and keep Google data out of training exports</a> — <strong>MERGED → master</strong> · 2026-11-25T01:57:24Z</p><h3 id="o27-·-paperclip-gates-native-swarms-behind-trusted-requests" tabindex="-1">O27 · Paperclip gates native swarms behind trusted requests <a class="header-anchor" href="#o27-·-paperclip-gates-native-swarms-behind-trusted-requests" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O27 · Paperclip gates native swarms behind trusted requests&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Merged master #22733 is off by default and requires a signed-in user&#39;s structured command plus server-recorded activity, not comment text; unavailable swarms fail explicitly. Native helpers are auto-approved, not sandboxed or shell-observable by Paperclip, and usage is aggregate. Live recipe cells lack an automated executor. High learning value with explicit governance blind spots; deepen main-radar coverage, no local trial.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22733" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#22733 feat(antigravity): trusted /swarm from the task composer, behind an experimental flag</a> — <strong>MERGED → master</strong> · 2026-11-25T01:54:24Z</p><h3 id="o28-·-paperclip-requalifies-stale-environments-without-bypass" tabindex="-1">O28 · Paperclip requalifies stale environments without bypass <a class="header-anchor" href="#o28-·-paperclip-requalifies-stale-environments-without-bypass" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O28 · Paperclip requalifies stale environments without bypass&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#22835 automatically probes stale snapshot proofs before lease admission, pins only after success, coalesces per-process probes and caches failure for two minutes; replicas do not share in-flight probes. #22734 reconciles pre-company managed rows and adds offline compatibility/incompatibility/invalid-evidence checks. Caller-supplied observations are not signed attestations. High operational learning and competitive relevance; no deployment validation here.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22835" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#22835 fix(runner): re-qualify a stale sandbox snapshot proof instead of blocking runs</a> — <strong>MERGED → master</strong> · 2026-11-24T23:19:33Z； <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22734" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#22734 Fix managed environment reconciliation and qualify runtimes before deployment</a> — <strong>MERGED → master</strong> · 2026-11-25T01:41:53Z</p><h3 id="o29-·-paperclip-bounds-repeated-dependency-wakes" tabindex="-1">O29 · Paperclip bounds repeated dependency wakes <a class="header-anchor" href="#o29-·-paperclip-bounds-repeated-dependency-wakes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O29 · Paperclip bounds repeated dependency wakes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#22818 reports 11,621 failed runs and 11,215 wakes over five days, each with a new blocked-cycle idempotency key. It adds 1m/5m/25m backoff up to 24h, reset by fresh dependency evidence/graph changes or nonfailed work. High long-running employee learning value; elevate recovery coverage. Counts are upstream incident reports, not local measurements or prevalence estimates.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22818" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#22818 fix(recovery): stop re-waking a blocked task whose dependency runs keep failing</a> — <strong>MERGED → master</strong> · 2026-11-24T21:25:26Z</p><h3 id="o30-·-paperclip-binds-quota-holds-to-credentials" tabindex="-1">O30 · Paperclip binds quota holds to credentials <a class="header-anchor" href="#o30-·-paperclip-binds-quota-holds-to-credentials" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O30 · Paperclip binds quota holds to credentials&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#22800 scopes quota holds to credentials, releasing stale waits when accounts change/revoke while keeping the same exhausted account held. Replies and Check now recheck retries, avoiding stale multi-day waits after reconnecting a working account. High learning value/moderate competitive risk; retain main radar. Account change must still be distinguished from authority continuity.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22800" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#22800 fix(heartbeat): a provider usage-limit hold applies only to the account that reported it</a> — <strong>MERGED → master</strong> · 2026-11-24T21:01:20Z</p><h3 id="o31-·-paperclip-recovers-accepted-replies-after-copy-back-failure" tabindex="-1">O31 · Paperclip recovers accepted replies after copy-back failure <a class="header-anchor" href="#o31-·-paperclip-recovers-accepted-replies-after-copy-back-failure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O31 · Paperclip recovers accepted replies after copy-back failure&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#22807 allows recovery of accepted done/needs_review replies for external-chat-woken nonconversation tasks after workspace copy-back failure, using the live path&#39;s authorization/source rules. Upstream previously reported refusal after six attempts. High learning/moderate competitive relevance; track delivery receipts. Reply recovery does not prove workspace synchronization or business acceptance.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22807" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#22807 fix(native-runtime): recover external-chat task replies skipped by copy-back failure</a> — <strong>MERGED → master</strong> · 2026-11-24T20:21:18Z</p><h3 id="o32-·-paperclip-corrects-budget-semantics" tabindex="-1">O32 · Paperclip corrects budget semantics <a class="header-anchor" href="#o32-·-paperclip-corrects-budget-semantics" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O32 · Paperclip corrects budget semantics&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Documentation-only #22784/#22833 clarifies that subscription usage adds zero billed dollars but existing scoped hard stops and per-run reserves still apply. Warning percentage is configurable; hard stop is an on/off 100% threshold. Unpriced-usage controls do not cover every unavailable-cost case. High semantic learning value, no capability upgrade inferred; keep radar assessment and test monetary/call/effect limits separately.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22784" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#22784 docs: describe budgets as they work today</a> — <strong>MERGED → master</strong> · 2026-11-24T22:25:26Z； <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22833" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#22833 docs: correct three budget claims from the review of the budget docs</a> — <strong>MERGED → master</strong> · 2026-11-24T22:45:35Z</p><h3 id="o33-·-paperclip-rejects-ambiguous-scoped-reset-requests" tabindex="-1">O33 · Paperclip rejects ambiguous scoped-reset requests <a class="header-anchor" href="#o33-·-paperclip-rejects-ambiguous-scoped-reset-requests" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O33 · Paperclip rejects ambiguous scoped-reset requests&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#19282 rejects blank taskKey with 400 rather than normalizing it to a global reset; omitted/null still explicitly requests all-task reset. A useful maintenance-scope distinction, moderate/high learning value without changing overall competitive maturity; retain on main radar.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/19282" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#19282 fix(agents): reject a blank taskKey on reset-session instead of resetting all task state</a> — <strong>MERGED → master</strong> · 2026-11-24T21:36:18Z</p><h3 id="o34-·-orca-distinguishes-no-answer-from-no-action" tabindex="-1">O34 · Orca distinguishes no answer from no action <a class="header-anchor" href="#o34-·-orca-distinguishes-no-answer-from-no-action" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O34 · Orca distinguishes no answer from no action&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#47901 warns when journaled tools may have acted; #47907 permits one same-chat answer-only retry only for a live single-request read-only turn with no posting attempt. Unknown tools are treated conservatively, and uncertain post outcomes block retry. Boot recovery, stopped and multi-request turns are excluded. High learning value; increase second-circle delivery/recovery attention. Not a blanket empty-answer retry.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/47901" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#47901 fix(connectors): a Slack turn with no answer says so plainly, and warns when tools already ran</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-25T01:06:52Z； <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/47907" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#47907 fix(bots): an empty Slack turn is asked once more before the thread hears there was no answer</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-25T01:52:15Z</p><h3 id="o35-·-orca-binds-answers-and-stop-to-current-targets" tabindex="-1">O35 · Orca binds answers and Stop to current targets <a class="header-anchor" href="#o35-·-orca-binds-answers-and-stop-to-current-targets" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O35 · Orca binds answers and Stop to current targets&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#48526 binds replies to the host&#39;s current questionEventId, refuses stale answers and restores drafts rather than retargeting them. #47951 rechecks live party/dispatch/settlement before Stop/Retry and invalidates held actions across feed loss. High governance learning value; deepen second-circle tracking, with no local cross-device validation.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/48526" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#48526 fix(items): recover an item reply refused for a replaced question on desktop and phone</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-25T00:14:02Z； <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/47951" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#47951 fix(dock): re-check Stop and Retry against the live dock, cancel held presses across a feed drop</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T05:07:57Z</p><h3 id="o36-·-orca-preserves-admission-time-reply-policy-across-upgrades" tabindex="-1">O36 · Orca preserves admission-time reply policy across upgrades <a class="header-anchor" href="#o36-·-orca-preserves-admission-time-reply-policy-across-upgrades" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O36 · Orca preserves admission-time reply policy across upgrades&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#48164 persists quiet_rule on pending Slack replies so live/restart paths honor admission-time semantics; records lacking it retain the old rule. High upgrade/recovery learning value, limited competitive evidence. It complements the SOP study: newer software does not automatically change an existing task&#39;s governing rule.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/48164" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#48164 Keep a quiet Slack bot reply quiet when Orca restarts mid-upgrade</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T09:17:16Z</p><h3 id="o37-·-orca-separates-account-access-actor-attribution-and-sharing-contracts" tabindex="-1">O37 · Orca separates account access, actor attribution and sharing contracts <a class="header-anchor" href="#o37-·-orca-separates-account-access-actor-attribution-and-sharing-contracts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O37 · Orca separates account access, actor attribution and sharing contracts&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#48238 restricts per-agent Google accounts and treats malformed lists as none, but absent legacy lists mean all and old hosts ignore lists. #48431 attributes owner actions only to appropriately stamped owner-only turns, excluding worker reports. #48246 is solely a sharing wire/encryption contract, with no serving/sending/reading implementation. High learning/competitive interest; retain second-circle classification with deeper governance coverage.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/48238" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#48238 feat(google): let agents use only the Google accounts chosen for them</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T18:15:51Z； <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/48431" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#48431 fix(connector): a turn the owner typed acts for the owner in Slack actions</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T21:14:02Z； <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/48246" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#48246 feat(sharing): contract for sharing an agent with Orca accounts</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T22:15:48Z</p><h3 id="o38-·-orca-prioritizes-provable-windows-stop-and-wsl-ownership" tabindex="-1">O38 · Orca prioritizes provable Windows Stop and WSL ownership <a class="header-anchor" href="#o38-·-orca-prioritizes-provable-windows-stop-and-wsl-ownership" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O38 · Orca prioritizes provable Windows Stop and WSL ownership&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#48073 forces per-chat Codex servers on Windows so Stop can terminate that chat&#39;s process tree, trading shared-server savings for isolation; other OSes are unchanged. #45247 stops rewriting user-owned WSL Codex config and regenerates a managed copy instead. High learning/moderate-high Windows competitive relevance; retain focused second-circle coverage, no installation/Stop test.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/48073" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#48073 Keep Windows Codex chats on their own server so Stop is accurate</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T09:52:41Z； <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/45247" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#45247 fix(codex): never write a WSL distro&#39;s Codex config; regenerate the managed copy from it</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T05:30:07Z</p><h3 id="o39-·-orca-adds-phone-side-identity-and-question-handling" tabindex="-1">O39 · Orca adds phone-side identity and question handling <a class="header-anchor" href="#o39-·-orca-adds-phone-side-identity-and-question-handling" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O39 · Orca adds phone-side identity and question handling&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#48266 lets phones request Slack posting-identity changes, still requiring installer approval; #48323 survives phone sleep during Google sign-in until link expiry; #47991 adds structured question answers. Released v1.4.273 advertises phone account/group controls, but later merges are not all claimed bundled. v1.4.274&#39;s app-rail UI alone is not a separate meaningful event. Moderate/high learning; deepen mobile governance coverage, untested on devices.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/48266" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#48266 feat(mobile): change who Slack replies post as from the phone</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T12:10:52Z； <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/48323" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#48323 fix(google): a Google sign-in started from the phone keeps waiting while the phone sleeps</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T13:55:02Z； <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/47991" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#47991 feat(mobile): answer an item&#39;s question in the chat&#39;s answer card</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T11:53:38Z； <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/releases/tag/v1.4.273" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v1.4.273</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-24T10:20:48Z</p><h3 id="o40-·-paradev-exposes-linux-delivery-and-retries-unreadable-history" tabindex="-1">O40 · Paradev exposes Linux delivery and retries unreadable history <a class="header-anchor" href="#o40-·-paradev-exposes-linux-delivery-and-retries-unreadable-history" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O40 · Paradev exposes Linux delivery and retries unreadable history&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Under the existing Superset→Paradev mapping, #10207 exposes experimental Linux x64 AppImage downloads, with OS-routing limitations and no newly verified stable Linux release. #9976 retains visible history and retries temporarily unreadable host journals with explicit states instead of blank-ready UI. Moderate/high learning and moderate desktop competition; keep main radar, installation/upgrade untested.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/10207" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#10207 feat(web): add Linux downloads to the web home and README</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T22:44:42Z； <a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9976" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#9976 fix(chat): keep a chat on screen and load its history again when the host cannot read it</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T15:55:56Z</p><h3 id="o41-·-crewai-clarifies-artifact-provenance-retrieval-and-caching" tabindex="-1">O41 · CrewAI clarifies artifact provenance, retrieval and caching <a class="header-anchor" href="#o41-·-crewai-clarifies-artifact-provenance-retrieval-and-caching" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O41 · CrewAI clarifies artifact provenance, retrieval and caching&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Released 1.15.45 adds PDF artifacts, disables save_artifact caching, drops cross-origin credentials and rejects empty authentication. Later #9733 adds a flow method name, not a unique ID; #9731 distinguishes AMP&#39;s one-day download URL from its authenticated viewer share_url, while local URLs stay file-based. Delivery, provenance and recipient retrieval need separate validation; not installed.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/releases/tag/1.15.45" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1.15.45</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-24T03:54:54Z； <a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/pull/9733" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#9733 feat(artifacts): name the flow method on ArtifactCreatedEvent </a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T19:32:16Z； <a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/pull/9731" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#9731 docs(artifacts): attach with url, link people with share_url</a> — <strong>MERGED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T16:48:59Z</p><h3 id="o42-·-langfuse-adds-trace-level-evaluation-and-mcp-evidence-views" tabindex="-1">O42 · Langfuse adds trace-level evaluation and MCP evidence views <a class="header-anchor" href="#o42-·-langfuse-adds-trace-level-evaluation-and-mcp-evidence-views" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O42 · Langfuse adds trace-level evaluation and MCP evidence views&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Released v4.85.0/v4.86.0 add trace-level transcript evaluation/testing/rules/UI, interactive MCP chart apps, native Responses tool-call ingestion and lost-trace dispatch accounting. Evaluator MCP tools hide transcript rules/mappings. Improved evaluation/inspection is not tamper-evident audit, independent acceptance or an FCoP implementation.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/releases/tag/v4.85.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v4.85.0</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-24T13:39:19Z； <a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/releases/tag/v4.86.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v4.86.0</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-24T18:54:46Z</p><h3 id="o43-·-github-mcp-expands-security-alert-mutation-tools" tabindex="-1">O43 · GitHub MCP expands security-alert mutation tools <a class="header-anchor" href="#o43-·-github-mcp-expands-security-alert-mutation-tools" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O43 · GitHub MCP expands security-alert mutation tools&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Released v2.3.0 adds update tools for Dependabot, code-scanning and secret-scanning alerts plus experimental PR artifact tools. Moving from reading to changing security disposition warrants identity/scope/reason/audit checks. No mutation tools were invoked here, and default token write authority is not assumed.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/releases/tag/v2.3.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v2.3.0</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-24T15:31:54Z</p><h3 id="o44-·-copilot-cli-prereleases-improve-cancellation-and-shared-auth" tabindex="-1">O44 · Copilot CLI prereleases improve cancellation and shared auth <a class="header-anchor" href="#o44-·-copilot-cli-prereleases-improve-cancellation-and-shared-auth" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O44 · Copilot CLI prereleases improve cancellation and shared auth&quot;">​</a></h3><p>v1.0.116-2 is a prerelease fixing repeated MCP sign-in across CLIs, idle-as-busy reconnect states, prompt cancellation delays, Unix shutdown-output cleanup and long-session cache growth; it warns on duplicate plugin/standalone endpoints. v1.0.115 is stable and includes orphan process-group stopping. No local upgrade validation.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/github/copilot-cli/releases/tag/v1.0.116-2" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v1.0.116-2</a> — <strong>RELEASED_PRERELEASE</strong> · 2026-11-25T00:12:08Z； <a href="https://github.com/github/copilot-cli/releases/tag/v1.0.115" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v1.0.115</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-24T13:03:50Z</p><h3 id="o45-·-gemini-cli-sanitizes-credential-prefixed-hook-names" tabindex="-1">O45 · Gemini CLI sanitizes credential-prefixed hook names <a class="header-anchor" href="#o45-·-gemini-cli-sanitizes-credential-prefixed-hook-names" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O45 · Gemini CLI sanitizes credential-prefixed hook names&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Default-branch #30448 sanitizes environment-assignment-prefixed hook names in OTEL bodies, attributes and metrics, rather than leaking credential text. It does not redact all hook content. Stable v0.71.1 cherry-picks yesterday&#39;s IPC-authentication fix #30420; the later hook change is not claimed bundled.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/commit/08e9a20f749aefcbda38622ac757899c3d6216e0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#30448 hook sanitization</a> — <strong>COMMITTED → main</strong> · 2026-11-24T23:51:44Z； <a href="https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/releases/tag/v0.71.1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v0.71.1</a> — <strong>RELEASED</strong> · 2026-11-24T03:50:24Z</p><h2 id="research-analysis" tabindex="-1">Research analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#research-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Research analysis&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="a1-·-priority-experiment-which-task-sop-and-grant-survives-handoff" tabindex="-1">A1 · Priority experiment: which task, SOP and grant survives handoff? <a class="header-anchor" href="#a1-·-priority-experiment-which-task-sop-and-grant-survives-handoff" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A1 · Priority experiment: which task, SOP and grant survives handoff?&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Evidence：O4、O5、O6、O25、O35、O36。</p><p>Evidence: parent evidence, durable cutoffs, current question IDs and admission-time policy constrain upstream decisions; StaffDeck separates SOP requirements from grants. A separate Nov 24 controlled CodeFlowMu/FCoP 4.0.5 study recorded 12 executions, 24 review judgments (12 formal reviews), one missing-source control, and a two-ticket migration pair: only the approved ticket adopted V2; neither repeated bank verification, and only that ticket repeated waiver execution/review once. These synthetic program-interpreted controls do not establish autonomous reasoning. Highest-value next trial: real worker/reviewer agents under version changes, pending/effective decisions, revocation, missing originals and shift identity changes. Requires retrievable originals and scoped decisions; costs include version retention and independent review. FCoP concerns traceable references/decisions/evidence; enforcement and cache invalidation belong to runtime/adapters. High-priority unrun experiment; engagement: invalidating resumed approval after evidence changes.</p><h3 id="a2-·-priority-experiment-recover-delivery-or-repeat-an-unknown-action" tabindex="-1">A2 · Priority experiment: recover delivery or repeat an unknown action? <a class="header-anchor" href="#a2-·-priority-experiment-recover-delivery-or-repeat-an-unknown-action" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A2 · Priority experiment: recover delivery or repeat an unknown action?&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Evidence：O8、O14、O18、O20、O29、O31、O34。</p><p>Evidence: MCP 404 recovery avoids replay, A2A sends once with unknown outcomes, and Orca gates empty-answer retries on effect evidence; Paperclip distinguishes accepted-result delivery loss from repeated blocked-cycle wakes. Inference: stable IDs, backoff, receipts and artifact retrieval must be combined; one idempotency key or successful run does not prove delivery. Candidate: count external effects under lost responses, crashes around report persistence, new/same attempts, deterministic dependency failure and revocation. Compare external executions, accepted results, delivery and acceptance separately. FCoP concerns attempt/report/receipt/unknown-result semantics; retry policy remains runtime. Requires independent external truth and fault injection; carries historical work, unrun. Engagement: querying an already-applied effect without resending it.</p><h3 id="a3-·-research-actor-identity-credentials-and-delegation-limits-separately" tabindex="-1">A3 · Research actor identity, credentials and delegation limits separately <a class="header-anchor" href="#a3-·-research-actor-identity-credentials-and-delegation-limits-separately" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A3 · Research actor identity, credentials and delegation limits separately&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Evidence：O3、O12、O13、O15、O16、O30、O37、O43。</p><p>Evidence separates session owner, allowed accounts, specialist routing and native child grants. OPEN community issue #6215 supplies a specific unchanged-bearer claim, not a universal finding. Quota-account change affects liveness without establishing task authority. Candidate: compare shared/per-specialist/exchanged tokens and revocation across tenants, accounts and same-name specialists; test concurrent shared-budget reservation, failed attempts and resume. OPEN #6211/#6212 remain design references. Requires identity/tool-service cooperation and token/audit costs. FCoP can compare delegation/responsibility evidence; credential issuance, pre-call authorization and rate limits belong to runtime/gateway. Unrun candidate/ongoing observation. Engagement: distinguish verifiable acting agent from represented user.</p><h3 id="a4-·-test-long-run-liveness-stop-and-evidence-delivery-independently" tabindex="-1">A4 · Test long-run liveness, Stop and evidence delivery independently <a class="header-anchor" href="#a4-·-test-long-run-liveness-stop-and-evidence-delivery-independently" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A4 · Test long-run liveness, Stop and evidence delivery independently&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Evidence：O19、O21、O22、O23、O35、O38、O44。</p><p>Evidence shows child waits misclassified as idle, state-lock waiters starving tools, slow webhooks retaining busy states and Windows shared servers lacking per-chat stop proof. /alive or green status cannot settle these. Candidate: real parent/child work plus subscription storms, slow webhooks and disconnected Stop; independently verify progress, stopped effects, readable history and late-event attribution. Isolation costs resources; heartbeat cannot replace atomic pause or orphan cleanup. FCoP concerns observable state/evidence relationships; process groups, pools, leases and idle policies are runtime. Unrun candidate. Engagement: verifiable cleanup of children outliving cancelled parents.</p><h3 id="a5-·-compose-protocol-layers-and-try-one-complete-job-workflow" tabindex="-1">A5 · Compose protocol layers and try one complete job workflow <a class="header-anchor" href="#a5-·-compose-protocol-layers-and-try-one-complete-job-workflow" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A5 · Compose protocol layers and try one complete job workflow&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Evidence：O1、O14、O24、O25、O27、O39、O40、O41、O42。</p><p>Evidence places Claude&#39;s skills/tasks/elicitation at tool-service workflow delivery, A2A at remote messaging/tasks, and FCoP at this project&#39;s file/artifact coordination contract. OpenHands boards and StaffDeck employee/SOP flows are application/runtime mechanisms, not all same-layer protocols. Experience candidates: pinned StaffDeck #325 and released OpenHands builds, after license/install/migration/recovery checks, covering assignment→human input→subtasks→report→review. Phone evaluation should assess approval/evidence/pause. Orca sharing remains contract-only; Paperclip swarm retains helper visibility/approval limits. Account, hosting terms and maintenance costs matter; source MIT does not establish service terms. None installed here; MCP&#39;s retrospective is background, not a new extension release.</p><h3 id="a6-·-deletion-redaction-signatures-and-audit-are-distinct-controls" tabindex="-1">A6 · Deletion, redaction, signatures and audit are distinct controls <a class="header-anchor" href="#a6-·-deletion-redaction-signatures-and-audit-are-distinct-controls" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A6 · Deletion, redaction, signatures and audit are distinct controls&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Evidence：O2、O9、O11、O17、O26、O41、O42、O45。</p><p>Evidence: SDK editors have explicit publication/object boundaries; ADK/Gemini show credentials escaping through separate telemetry paths; Paperclip extends deletion across handoffs and training copies; signatures validate origin/integrity, not behavior. Candidate: synthetic markers across raw/structured/meta results, traces, replay, upgrades and exports; map derived copies and reconcile revocation deletion with minimal audit evidence. FCoP can study artifact provenance/derivation and retained evidence summaries; runtime/connectors enforce deletion/redaction. A hash proves neither retrievability, confidentiality nor legal compliance. Costs include lineage and scanning; scoped negative controls first. Unrun candidate. Engagement: minimal facts retained after deleting result content.</p><h2 id="carryover-reconciliation" tabindex="-1">Carryover reconciliation <a class="header-anchor" href="#carryover-reconciliation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Carryover reconciliation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Fresh main was compared with the Nov24 monitoring commit, establishing a separately executed/published Nov24 SOP-handoff study. This is reconciliation, not an experiment run today or a rewrite of yesterday&#39;s snapshot.</p><p><a href="./../../research/2026-11-24-sop-version-handoff">SOP handoff study and public evidence</a></p><p>Pinned CodeFlowMu 0d2d4e742ef2f3cb48e3ce09cc47f0c03053dc5f and FCoP/FCoP MCP 4.0.5. Initial controls: 12 executions,24 review judgments (12 formal reviews),one missing-original case. Two-ticket follow-up: only approved work adopted the new SOP, both retained bank verification, only approved work repeated waiver execution/review. Synthetic inputs/test identities through real product interfaces, with program-interpreted policy and no LLM. Review stage is not business acceptance. Unchanged result bytes do not prove unchanged premises.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Original date + ID</th><th>Disposition</th><th>Evidence and remaining work</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2026-11-19 A1</td><td>Pending</td><td>Retain November 19 scoped skill-boundary results; not rerun, live mounting/authority/execution remain pending. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-19 A2</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending: upstream/document checks only; original experiments not run. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-19 A3</td><td>Partially completed; remaining pending</td><td>Retain Nov22/23 scoped evidence; separate Nov24 work adds controlled version/formal-review/selective-migration paths (12 executions,24 judgments,one missing-source control,two-ticket follow-up). Program-interpreted synthetic controls; autonomous reasoning,live-host handoff and business acceptance remain pending; not rerun today.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-19 A4</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending: upstream/document checks only; original experiments not run. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-19 A5</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending: upstream/document checks only; original experiments not run. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-19 A6</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending: upstream/document checks only; original experiments not run. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-19 A7</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending: upstream/document checks only; original experiments not run. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-17 A2</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; retain historical stop regressions; external-effect/lost-receipt tests remain unrun. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-17 A4</td><td>Partially completed; remaining pending</td><td>Retain Nov22/23 scoped evidence; separate Nov24 work adds controlled version/formal-review/selective-migration paths (12 executions,24 judgments,one missing-source control,two-ticket follow-up). Program-interpreted synthetic controls; autonomous reasoning,live-host handoff and business acceptance remain pending; not rerun today.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-16 A1</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; real dual-host takeover unrun. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-16 A2</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; real Core/ACP trials unrun. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-22 A1</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; retry authority/resource/budget experiments unrun. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-22 A2</td><td>Partially completed; remaining pending</td><td>Retain Nov22/23 scoped evidence; separate Nov24 work adds controlled version/formal-review/selective-migration paths (12 executions,24 judgments,one missing-source control,two-ticket follow-up). Program-interpreted synthetic controls; autonomous reasoning,live-host handoff and business acceptance remain pending; not rerun today.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-22 A3</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; failed-governance-check and credential negative controls unrun. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-22 A4</td><td>Pending</td><td>Document review advanced: Orca source MIT verified; product/isolation/hosted terms remain pending. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-22 A5</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; install/migration/recovery/event/upgrade trials unrun. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-23 A1</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; document updates do not replace the experiment. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-23 A2</td><td>Partially completed; remaining pending</td><td>Retain Nov22/23 scoped evidence; separate Nov24 work adds controlled version/formal-review/selective-migration paths (12 executions,24 judgments,one missing-source control,two-ticket follow-up). Program-interpreted synthetic controls; autonomous reasoning,live-host handoff and business acceptance remain pending; not rerun today.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-23 A3</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; document updates do not replace the experiment. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-23 A4</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; document updates do not replace the experiment. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-23 A5</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; document updates do not replace the experiment. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-23 A6</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; document updates do not replace the experiment. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-24 A1</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; monitoring does not replace the original experience/experiment. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-24 A2</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; monitoring does not replace the original experience/experiment. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-24 A3</td><td>Partially completed; remaining pending</td><td>Retain Nov22/23 scoped evidence; separate Nov24 work adds controlled version/formal-review/selective-migration paths (12 executions,24 judgments,one missing-source control,two-ticket follow-up). Program-interpreted synthetic controls; autonomous reasoning,live-host handoff and business acceptance remain pending; not rerun today.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-24 A4</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; monitoring does not replace the original experience/experiment. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-24 A5</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending; monitoring does not replace the original experience/experiment. Original experiment not run this round.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>New experiments today:0; new articles today:0; development reviews:0; comments sent:0. One prior-day independent article was reconciled (its bilingual mirrors are one outcome), not counted again as today&#39;s production. Candidates remain unexecuted and create no development tasks.</p><h2 id="cross-project-synthesis-and-source-coverage" tabindex="-1">Cross-project synthesis and source coverage <a class="header-anchor" href="#cross-project-synthesis-and-source-coverage" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Cross-project synthesis and source coverage&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The fresh Registry contains 47 researchers and 35 engineering repositories; the supplemental technical/competitor union has 88 original repository entries. The verified Superset-to-Paradev mapping is retained without Registry edits. Researchers remain subjects, repositories many-to-many evidence entrances. Preserve all six governance relationships; bulbasaur is not an official AGENTSAFE artifact. No dated new Zhao paper announcement was independently established in the checked homepage/repository increments; that is not exhaustive author coverage.</p><p>Eighty-five commit-query windows completed. Paperclip/Orca historical pagination remains incomplete, retaining their old successful baselines. Orca&#39;s separate recent-window scan reached page three (268 commits); recent-window completion does not close older history. TSA commits/issues/releases remain inaccessible. The 176 Issues/Release samples used 30 entries/page; full pages remain partial. Codex release-list calls failed twice with Transport closed; latest-release succeeded and stable 0.172.0 predates this window, which does not complete release-list coverage. Historical classification queues remain pending. Discussions, roadmaps, security advisories, all 47 researchers&#39; social activity and all licensing/hosting terms were not exhaustively reviewed.</p><p>Separate non-GitHub checks: Claude&#39;s Nov24 announcement; MCP&#39;s Nov24 retrospective and current Events/Skills docs; Cursor changelog and product release timeline (latest visible Nov20, outside window); Zhao&#39;s homepage; official-domain searches. Historical Events/Skills status is background, not counted again. X/replies/threads are not exhaustive. GitHub primary engineering evidence can stand alone; two GitHub links are not two source types. Many Codex changes use copyberry projections, which do not establish direct original-author involvement; named SDK/StaffDeck PR authors are inspectable but do not imply local testing.</p><p>Only today&#39;s bilingual reports and indexes are updated; no research/runtime/**, article or lifecycle mutation. Sources are reread after commit. The existing site implementation and snapshots are retained; actual source/build/deployment/click verification is recorded separately in local publication receipts.</p>',169)])])}const g=a(i,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
